  "title": "How Therapy Can Benefit Communities of Color",
  "summary": "The average black person considers mental illness a weakness and so avoids acknowledging the problem and seeking help. Also, many Asian cultures keep mental health issues within the family, as seeking external help may bring shame and soil their reputation. These issues are also prevalent among the Hispanic community, which prioritizes self-reliance and stoicism. But […]",
